-- reply: sender and all recipients, without me
"$TMP/sys": 2 messages 2 new
To: Alice <alice@a.example>, root@here, bob@b.example
Cc: carol@c.example
Subject: Re: plans
Held 2 messages in $TMP/sys
== sendmail -oi -- alice@a.example ME@here bob@b.example carol@c.example
To: Alice <alice@a.example>, ME@here, bob@b.example
Cc: carol@c.example
Subject: Re: plans
Date: DATE
In-Reply-To: <p1@a.example>
References: <p1@a.example>

thanks
-- Reply: the sender only
"$TMP/sys": 2 messages 2 unread
To: Alice <alice@a.example>
Subject: Re: plans
== sendmail -oi -- alice@a.example
To: Alice <alice@a.example>
Subject: Re: plans
Date: DATE
In-Reply-To: <p1@a.example>
References: <p1@a.example>

thanks
-- Reply-To replaces From; Re: is not doubled
"$TMP/sys": 2 messages 2 unread
To: list@l.example, other@o.example
Subject: Re: plans
== sendmail -oi -- list@l.example other@o.example
To: list@l.example, other@o.example
Subject: Re: plans
Date: DATE

ok
-- Reply to several messages
"$TMP/sys": 2 messages 2 unread
To: Alice <alice@a.example>, list@l.example
Subject: Re: plans
== sendmail -oi -- alice@a.example list@l.example
To: Alice <alice@a.example>, list@l.example
Subject: Re: plans
Date: DATE
In-Reply-To: <p1@a.example>
References: <p1@a.example>

both
-- flipr swaps them
"$TMP/sys": 2 messages 2 unread
To: Alice <alice@a.example>
Subject: Re: plans
== sendmail -oi -- alice@a.example
To: Alice <alice@a.example>
Subject: Re: plans
Date: DATE
In-Reply-To: <p1@a.example>
References: <p1@a.example>

flipped
-- metoo keeps me
"$TMP/sys": 2 messages 2 unread
To: list@l.example, root, other@o.example
Subject: Re: plans
== sendmail -oi -- list@l.example ME other@o.example
-- alternates are removed
"$TMP/sys": 2 messages 2 unread
To: list@l.example
Subject: Re: plans
== sendmail -oi -- list@l.example
-- followup records in a file named after the author
1
